{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>The da'ah.</b> Oiseau de proie (bird of prey), from the root of ידאה הנשר. And your mnemonic: דש חטין — explained: the da'ah is visible, in the portion שמיני." "<b>The ayah.</b> Rabbi Akiva said: ״איה״ is stated here and ״דיה״ is stated elsewhere; just as ״דיה״ stated elsewhere — make from it the ראה (reish) in the portion ראה, and your mnemonic: רר בשרו, a species of ayah — so too ״איה״ stated here: make from it the דאה (dalet), a species of ayah. And because its habit is to dwell in islands (איים), it is called איה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The Old French gloss וושטויי״‎ר is rendered here as 'bird of prey' based on medieval French osto(o)r/oxtor, a hawk-type raptor; the exact identification is approximate.", 1 "The rabbinic derivation involves reassigning letters: 'ayah' here is read as 'da'ah' by replacing alef-yod with dalet; the mnemonic strings (דש חטין / רר בשרו) are preserved as given despite their obscurity."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:18.804090366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}